    <string name="faq_title">FAQ</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">Where is my data stored?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Only on your phone. Dallet has no internet access, no accounts and no servers: nobody but you can see your money.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">What happens to my data if my phone breaks or is lost?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">Open More, then Auto backups, pick a folder (for example on Google Drive or an SD card) and turn on the daily copy. The last 7 copies are kept. On a new phone restore with Import.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">How do I move my data to another phone?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">On the old phone: More, then Export, and save the file. On the new one install Dallet and use More, then Import (or Restore from file on the first launch) to pick that file.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">I forgot the backup password. What now?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">The password is not stored anywhere by the developer, so it cannot be recovered. A backup without a password, or an older one with another password, still opens. Keep the password somewhere safe.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">What is the difference between From account and As income when adding to a goal?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">From account: the money is taken from the chosen account and set aside in the goal, so the account balance drops. As income: the money came from outside (a gift, a bonus) and goes straight into the goal. It counts as income in Analytics, and the account balance stays the same.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">How does a purchase work?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">Make a list, tick what you bought and enter prices. Closing the purchase creates one expense on the chosen account for the ticked items, and the prices go into the price history. Unticked items can be moved to a new list.</string>
    <string name="faq_q7">Can I change a closed purchase or its expense?</string>
    <string name="faq_a7">The amount of a purchase expense cannot be edited: it equals the list total. To fix it, tap Reopen in the purchase: the expense is removed, the balance comes back, fix the list and close it again.</string>
    <string name="faq_q8">How do currencies and rates work?</string>
    <string name="faq_a8">All amounts are kept in the main currency (change it in More, then Settings). In Rates and converter you enter rates by hand, and the Convert button turns an amount from another currency into the main one.</string>
    <string name="faq_q9">What are Due and recurring operations?</string>
    <string name="faq_a9">A recurring operation (rent, a subscription, salary) repeats on a schedule. When it is due it appears on the home screen in Due, and you confirm or skip it. A reminder comes at about 9:00.</string>
    <string name="faq_q10">What if I forget the PIN?</string>
    <string name="faq_a10">The PIN is stored only on the phone and cannot be recovered. So turn on auto backups in advance: if you have to reinstall the app, the data comes back from a copy.</string>
