    <string name="faq_q13">How do I track a loan or an instalment plan?</string>
    <string name="faq_a13">Create a regular operation (More → Regular operations) of the Expense type. If you know the payment, enter it and choose “Every month”. If you only know the total, switch to “Calculate until”, enter the total and pick a term (3, 6, 9, 12, 24 months or your own date): the app works out the payment. Each payment shows up in “To pay”, you confirm it, and the list shows “8 of 12 payments left”. After the last payment the rule is marked “Finished”.</string>
    <string name="faq_q14">What do the blocks on the home screen show?</string>
    <string name="faq_a14">Shopping, Goals, Debts and Regular operations show three items each. Tap an item to open that list, goal, debt or rule right away, for example to add money to a goal. The “All …” button at the bottom of a block opens the whole section.</string>
    <string name="faq_q15">Why does the app warn about a negative balance?</string>
    <string name="faq_a15">When a goal deposit, or lending or repaying a debt, would take an account below zero, Dallet asks you to confirm. If you are sure, tap “Continue anyway”; if not, cancel and pick another account.</string>
    <string name="faq_q16">Are goals and debts in the report?</string>
    <string name="faq_a16">Yes. The PDF and CSV report (Analytics → export report) lists goals with their progress and unsettled debts with what is left after the totals. They are shown as of today and do not depend on the chosen period.</string>
    <string name="faq_q17">Why does the app ask before deleting?</string>
    <string name="faq_a17">So that a stray tap cannot wipe data. Every deletion (an operation, account, category, budget, regular operation, shopping item) first shows a “Delete?” dialog. A deleted item can only be restored from a backup.</string>
